  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Women and Youth Initiatives organization is a community-based organization founded in 2019 by a group of fifteen Mwanza-based women. The primary goal was to improve the economic standing of young mothers and women, as well as to provide young girls, mothers, and women with sexual and reproductive health rights. WnY &#xa0;were finally officially registered in 2021 with the registration number MCC/CD/SHG/430, after having received several setbacks in their&#xa0;operation, for which they&#xa0;were required by law to be registered in order to conduct our activities.  &#xa0;WnY&#xa0;were able to draft a constitution that&#xa0;serves as the foundation for their&#xa0;community-based organization and all of their&#xa0;activities. The headquarters are located in Mwanza, in the nyamagana neighborhood, at house number 030/495.WnY &#xa0;organization, according to their&#xa0;constitution, is a non-profit organization with 15 members; however, they&#xa0;serve a large community of young mothers and women in Mirongo ward in Nyamagana district. This community is locatedin the Mwanza Lake Zone of Nyamagana. WnY&apos;s primary goals are to increase awareness and provide training on
sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR), teach young
mothers and women skills in leadership and confidence, vocational
training and entrepreneur skills, establishing a community bank in the
village, and organize activities that generate cash for the group.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and Youth Initiatives</narrative>
  </participating-org>
